  "releaseNotes": "Type-narrowing assertion: Is().A<T>() (synonym Is().An<T>()) asserts the object is of type T (subtypes accepted) and exposes it, strongly typed, through 'that' — `var encounter = one.Is().A<EncounterComposition>().that;` — combining the type check and cast in one step. Renders as \"one is a EncounterComposition\"; 'that' after an inverted `not.A<T>()` throws SetupFailed. Has().Type<T>() is now deprecated in favor of Is().A<T>()",
